{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfZboxuFyfXgNUrQtDJvz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Repository findings:**\n- Shipment entity at: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt:9-14`\n- ShipmentStatus enum at: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt:23-27`\n- ShipmentController at: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt:20-56`\n- InMemoryShipmentRepository at: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentRepository.kt:10-27`\n- Exception handling at: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiExceptions.kt:11-24`\n- ErrorCode enum at: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt:31-37`\n\n**Conventions this repository follows:**\n1. Controller methods throw `ApiException` subclasses (ConflictException, ResourceNotFoundException) rather than returning error responses\n2. Each error condition has a machine-readable `ErrorCode` in the enum\n3. GlobalExceptionHandler centrally converts exceptions to `ApiError` envelope with code, message, and fields\n4. 404 uses `ResourceNotFoundException` with `NOT_FOUND` status\n5. 409 uses `ConflictException` with `CONFLICT` status\n6. Tests use MockMvc with assertions on status codes and JSON paths\n7. Repository methods return `Shipment?` (nullable) for lookups\n8. Update operations modify a copy and call `save()` on the repository\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ShipmentController.kt` - Must add the new POST endpoint for confirm\n2. `ShipmentRepository.kt` - May need to add an update method (or use save(), which already does update)\n3. `ApiError.kt` - Must add new ErrorCode for the CANCELLED rejection case (this is supporting infrastructure for the feature)\n4. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` - Must add tests for all four cases\n\n**Risks:**\n1. Idempotency: confirming an already-CONFIRMED shipment must not fail - need to ensure the logic checks status before throwing\n2. Persistence: the repository stores the updated shipment correctly\n3. Status transition: only CREATED → CONFIRMED transition should succeed; CONFIRMED → CONFIRMED should be no-op; CANCELLED → CONFIRMED should fail\n\n**Open questions:**\nNone that change the correct behavior - the ticket clearly specifies what each case should do.\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt**: Add new error code `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS` to the ErrorCode enum for the CANCELLED shipment case\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt**: Add new endpoint:\n   ```kotlin\n   @PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")\n   fun confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String): Shipment {\n       // Get the shipment or throw 404\n       val shipment = repository.findById(shipmentId) \n           ?: throw ResourceNotFoundException(...)\n       \n       // If already CONFIRMED, return as-is (idempotent)\n       if (shipment.status == ShipmentStatus.CONFIRMED) {\n           return shipment\n       }\n       \n       // If CANCELLED, throw 409 conflict\n       if (shipment.status == ShipmentStatus.CANCELLED) {\n           throw ConflictException(...)\n       }\n       \n       // If CREATED, transition to CONFIRMED and save\n       val confirmed = shipment.copy(status = ShipmentStatus.CONFIRMED)\n       return repository.save(confirmed)\n   }\n   ```\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add four new tests covering:\n   - Confirming a CREATED shipment transitions to CONFIRMED\n   - Confirming an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds with no change (idempotent)\n   - Confirming a CANCELLED shipment returns 409 with appropriate error code\n   - Confirming a non-existent shipment returns 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n\n**Alternative approaches rejected:**\n- Could have used a service layer (ShipmentService) between controller and repository, but this adds unnecessary complexity and doesn't match the existing architecture which has controllers call repositories directly\n- Could have added a dedicated `confirmShipment()` method to the repository, but this is less necessary since the status change is simple and a `copy()` + `save()` is clear\n- Could have reused an existing error code like VALIDATION_FAILED for the CANCELLED case, but this is semantically incorrect and confuses clients\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Input | Logic | HTTP | Response Body | Persisted |\n|------|-------|-------|------|---|---|\n| CREATED → CONFIRMED | shipmentId=S-1, status=CREATED | fetch, check status, copy with CONFIRMED, save | 200 | Shipment with status=CONFIRMED | Yes |\n| CONFIRMED → CONFIRMED (idempotent) | shipmentId=S-1, status=CONFIRMED | fetch, check status, return as-is | 200 | Shipment with status=CONFIRMED | No |\n| CANCELLED → ? | shipmentId=S-1, status=CANCELLED | fetch, check status, throw ConflictException | 409 | {error: {code: SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS, message: \"...\"}} | No |\n| Unknown ID | shipmentId=missing | fetch returns null, throw ResourceNotFoundException | 404 | {error: {code: SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, message: \"...\"}} | No |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n1. `confirmCreatedShipment()`: Create S-confirm-1 in CREATED status, POST confirm, expect 200 with CONFIRMED status\n2. `confirmIdempotently()`: Create S-confirm-2 in CREATED, POST confirm twice, both succeed with 200 and CONFIRMED\n3. `rejectCancelledShipment()`: Manually insert shipment in CANCELLED status, POST confirm, expect 409 with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS error code\n4. `rejectUnknownShipment()`: POST confirm on non-existent ID, expect 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND error code\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nLet me start by adding the error code:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":561,"cache_read_input_tokens":20929,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input