{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfZbrVw7pab5gUZULXvXj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! All tests passed. **Command:** `./mvnw test` from `sample-service/`. **Result:** BUILD SUCCESS with 17 tests (9 shipment tests: 5 existing + 4 new). **Failures:** None.\n\n<<PHASE:REVIEW>>\n\nLet me verify the implementation against the requirements:\n\n**Acceptance criteria mapping:**\n1. ✅ Existing build passes - BuildSUCCESS with all existing tests passing\n2. ✅ Existing tests pass - OrderControllerTest (4), SampleServiceApplicationTests (1), CustomerControllerTest (3) all pass\n3. ✅ `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` confirms a created shipment and persists it - test `confirmCreatedShipment` verifies this\n4. ✅ Error responses consistent with API - uses same ConflictException and ResourceNotFoundException pattern as existing code, error envelope from GlobalExceptionHandler\n5. ✅ Repeated confirm succeeds; cancelled shipment refused; unknown id refused - covered by tests `confirmIdempotently`, `rejectCancelledShipment`, `rejectUnknownShipment`\n6. ✅ No new Maven dependency - only added Kotlin code, no pom.xml changes\n7. ✅ No unrelated production file changes - only touched ShipmentController, ShipmentRepository is used as-is, ApiError.kt addition is required for proper error handling\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** - Added `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS` error code to enum. This is necessary infrastructure for the feature and consistent with the API's error code pattern.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** - Added confirm endpoint that:\n   - Throws ResourceNotFoundException (404) if shipment not found ✅\n   - Returns shipment unchanged (200) if already CONFIRMED (idempotent) ✅\n   - Throws ConflictException (409) with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS if CANCELLED ✅\n   - Transitions CREATED to CONFIRMED, saves, and returns (200) ✅\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Added four tests:\n   - `confirmCreatedShipment()` - covers CREATED → CONFIRMED transition\n   - `confirmIdempotently()` - covers CONFIRMED → CONFIRMED idempotency\n   - `rejectCancelledShipment()` - covers CANCELLED rejection with 409\n   - `rejectUnknownShipment()` - covers unknown ID rejection with 404\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. The implementation is complete and correct.\n\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n\n```\nRequirement   Add POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm endpoint that transitions CREATED shipments to CONFIRMED, handles idempotent retries, rejects CANCELLED with 409, and unknown IDs with 404\nChanged       ApiError.kt - Added SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS error code to ErrorCode enum\n              ShipmentController.kt - Added confirm endpoint with status validation and persistence logic\n              ShipmentControllerTest.kt - Added 4 tests covering CREATED→CONFIRMED, idempotency, CANCELLED rejection, and 404 cases\nTests         confirmCreatedShipment - verifies CREATED transitions to CONFIRMED and returns 200\n              confirmIdempotently - verifies calling confirm twice on same shipment succeeds both times (idempotent)\n              rejectCancelledShipment - verifies CANCELLED shipment returns 409 with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS error code\n              rejectUnknownShipment - verifies missing shipment returns 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND error code\nVerification  Command: ./mvnw test from sample-service/\n              Result: BUILD SUCCESS - 17 tests passed (9 shipment: 5 existing + 4 new, 4 order, 1 app, 3 customer)\nNot done      Nothing - all requirements satisfied and all tests passing\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2966,"cache_read_input_tokens":25381,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2966},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"contex